dependency-lock.json records exact commits and hashes of integration inputs.
prepare_sources.py produces modified sources in the build directory; it removes
upstream's entry point, adds a reset/dispatch API, limits FFTs to 512 bins, reports
USB-only transport, binds the sniffer packet pool to shared SRAM, and gates BLE writes.
It also preserves ownership of the sniffer's static BLE server callback and checks
SDK NimBLE host initialization before launching the host task. sdk_host.h selects
the SDK host headers for the Arduino C++ wrappers so only the SDK initializes the
controller. The pinned dependency source trees are not edited.

When distributing a binary, provide its corresponding source: this directory,
the exact wlc_sniffer.ino identified in source-manifest.json, pinned dependency
sources and their license files, sdkconfig, and build scripts. Preserve the
generated source manifest and generated sources with the binary. This notice
does not turn a binary-only delivery into a source-compliant distribution.

This variant also renames seven RF-test BSS scratch sections in a PRIVATE SDK
copy. Code, symbols, relocations and sizes are preserved. Include
prepare_rf_archive.py and its archive transformation manifest as build inputs.
